# MEMORY — Lessons · Facts · Asks
*The single always-loaded memory file (one file, three sections). Read IN FULL by every mentor agent and at every DOMAIN_SESSION PREPARE.*

> **Why this file exists.** A mentor system that records its mistakes in files the plan-generating agent never reads is not learning — it is keeping a diary. This file puts the system's own corrections, facts, and open asks **into the generation path**, so a correction given in week N provably changes behaviour in week N+1. It is deliberately small; keeping it small is a hard requirement, not a nicety.
>
> **The three sections and their one-line jobs:**
> - **LESSONS** — every correction the user gives becomes a pre-flight RULE. Read by every mentor before it drafts.
> - **FACTS** — binding facts + a Never-Repeat list. A plan that contradicts a fact is wrong by definition.
> - **ASKS** — an open-ask ledger with mechanical, age-based escalation, so a persistent unmet ask escalates itself instead of quietly persisting.

---

## LESSONS — The Mistake→Lesson Loop
*The always-loaded correction memory.*

> **What this file is.** Every correction {{USER_NAME}} gives becomes a RULE here, phrased as a pre-flight check. This section is READ BY EVERY MENTOR AGENT and at every DOMAIN_SESSION PREPARE — it is in the generation path, which is the whole point. The failure it prevents: a correction recorded only in `coordinator_state.md` / `profile.md` / a domain `log.md` that the weekly mentor agents never read, so the same root cause fires again and again.
>
> **Write rule.** Any principal correction (a "this is wrong" flag, a factual error caught, a "weakly planned / mundane" rebuke, a contradicted fact) MUST produce a new lesson or increment an existing lesson's violation count **in the same JOURNAL/review pass**. No correction leaves the session unrecorded.
>
> **Enforcement.** Each mentor report answers the PRE-FLIGHT questions in its PREFLIGHT section (one line each: pass / fail+fix). Unanswered = report incomplete and regenerated.
>
> **Recurrence escalation.** If a lesson's violation count reaches 2 after adoption, the lesson's phrasing has failed — the fix must become STRUCTURAL (a protocol edit, a curriculum edit, a file-format change), not another prose reminder. Note the escalation here.
>
> **Size cap.** ≤ 40 active lessons / ~150 lines. At each SEASON_TRANSITION: retire lessons absorbed into protocol/curriculum (move to `coordinator_history/<YYYY>.md` with a tombstone), merge duplicates, delete wrong ones.

