## FACTS — Durable Fact & Never-Repeat Ledger
*The always-loaded ground-truth memory.*

> **What this file is.** The short list of load-bearing facts {{USER_NAME}} has stated that a fresh-drafted plan must never contradict, plus the Never-Repeat list of declined items. READ BY EVERY MENTOR AGENT and at every DOMAIN_SESSION PREPARE. Forgetting failures (re-proposing done work, re-asserting a corrected fact, re-serving a declined item) happen because facts live only in prose the drafting agent doesn't reread, or get overridden by a fresh draft.
>
> **Write rule.** When {{USER_NAME}} states a fact that (a) contradicts something the system assumed, or (b) closes off a direction, add one line here in the same pass. Facts are dated. When a fact is superseded, edit it in place and note the change — never leave two versions (that is the drift P8 forbids).
>
> **This is a POINTER layer, not a second source of truth.** Each fact names its canonical home file. FACTS exists so the drafting agent reliably *sees* the fact cheaply; the detailed version lives in its home. Keep entries to one line. DRIFT_CHECK reconciles each fact against its home every week.
>
> **Size cap.** ~40 facts. Retire facts that are no longer live (season over, decision executed) at SEASON_TRANSITION.

