## ASKS — Open Request Ledger & Escalation Board
*The self-escalating signal tracker.*

> **Canonical ownership (P8).** This section is the SINGLE canonical ledger for open recurring asks and their ages. `coordinator_state.md` may reference an ask for cross-domain context but does not re-track its age/owner/status. One ask, one home.
>
> **What this file is.** Every explicit ask {{USER_NAME}} makes that isn't closeable in one week gets a row here with the date first raised and an owner. READ BY THE COORDINATOR at every WEEKLY_REVIEW Phase 1; its OPEN high-age rows are surfaced at Checkpoint 1 automatically. This fixes the worst signal failure: a persistent unmet ask that quietly persists for weeks because it has no home that forces attention.
>
> **The escalation rule (mechanical, not judgment).**
> - **Age 0–1 review:** normal — an owner is assigned, a deliverable named.
> - **Age 2 reviews unmet:** ESCALATE. An existing mentor is named owner with a specific weekly deliverable. Surfaced at Checkpoint 1 as an escalation, not a status line.
> - **Age 3+ reviews unmet:** BLOCKING. It becomes a mandatory Mentor Challenge at Checkpoint 2 — the coordinator must present why it keeps failing and propose a structural change (drop it, change owner, or change the approach). An ask cannot silently persist past age 3.
>
> **Close rule.** An ask closes ONLY with a shipped artifact + {{USER_NAME}}'s explicit confirmation. "Owner assigned" is not closed. "Mentor thinks it's handled" is not closed. Self-declared resolution is prohibited.
>
> **Write rule.** Add a row the moment an ask is stated. Increment `Age` (in reviews) every WEEKLY_REVIEW it stays open. Never delete an open ask; move closed ones to the Closed table with the closing artifact named.

